From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mowsoon <Mowsoon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] preload: skip restarts only while Discord shares audio

The hook keeps the LocalUser objects that received a successful
SignalOnSoundshare(true) in a set, and removes them only on
SignalOnSoundshare(false). In Discord 1.0.168 a soundshare also ends
through LocalUser::SignalOnSoundshareEnded(), which clears the state
without calling SignalOnSoundshare(false). The object then stays in
the set, and the next legitimate start of the same LocalUser is
suppressed, which leaves the stream without audio. A LocalUser
allocated at the address of a freed one hits the same problem.

Read Discord's own soundshare state instead. SignalOnSoundshare()
stores its argument in a byte of LocalUser and
SignalOnSoundshareEnded() clears that byte. Take the offset of the
byte from these two stores, 0x1f30 in Discord 1.0.168, and leave the
function unpatched when either store is missing or when they disagree.
A start is suppressed only while the byte says that a soundshare is
already active.
---
 native/preload.cc | 80 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 59 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/native/preload.cc b/native/preload.cc
index 8b85034..3c1cfe0 100644
--- a/native/preload.cc
+++ b/native/preload.cc
@@ -21,7 +21,6 @@
